        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): bound IDENTITY.md reads to prevent OOM",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`loadIdentityFromFile` in `src/agents/identity-file.ts` loaded `IDENTITY.md` with `fs.readFileSync(..., \"utf-8\")` and no size cap. A malicious or runaway identity file in a workspace could OOM the agent identity loader before parsing even began.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nIdentity files are small human-authored markdown, so the existing shared workspace bootstrap cap (`MAX_WORKSPACE_BOOTSTRAP_FILE_BYTES`, 2 MiB, exported from `src/agents/workspace.ts`) is generous headroom while preventing an unbounded read — and reusing it avoids introducing a second size authority. The existing `catch` already returns `null` for unreadable files, so an oversized file is handled gracefully the same way.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Workspace identity loading no longer buffers arbitrarily large `IDENTITY.md` files.\n- Oversized identity files are treated as missing (returns `null`) instead of crashing.\n- Normal identity files work exactly as before.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact head: `df0d51978c1cb7e3a3b83e0d6df1d5e50006eed7` (`fix(agents): reuse shared workspace bootstrap file size limit for IDENTITY.md`).\n\n- `loadIdentityFromFile` in `src/agents/identity-file.ts` now reads via `readRegularFileSync({ filePath, maxBytes: MAX_WORKSPACE_BOOTSTRAP_FILE_BYTES })`, reusing the shared 2 MiB workspace bootstrap limit; read failures and oversized files flow through the existing `null` fallback.\n- Regression tests in `src/agents/identity-file.test.ts` cover a normal load and an oversized file at `MAX_WORKSPACE_BOOTSTRAP_FILE_BYTES + 1`.\n\n### Standalone terminal proof (exact head, outside Vitest)\n\nA Node/tsx script imports the changed loader (`loadAgentIdentityFromWorkspace`) and the shared limit directly from source at this head, then exercises a normal file, a file exactly at the 2 MiB cap, and a file one byte over the cap in a throwaway `/tmp` workspace (fixtures deleted after the run; private paths redacted):\n\n```text\n$ node -v && git rev-parse HEAD\nv24.15.0\ndf0d51978c1cb7e3a3b83e0d6df1d5e50006eed7\n\n$ tsx proof-101447.mjs\nMAX_WORKSPACE_BOOTSTRAP_FILE_BYTES = 2097152 (2 MiB)\n\n=== Normal IDENTITY.md (59 bytes) ===\nResult: {\n  \"name\": \"Proof Agent\",\n  \"emoji\": \"🧪\",\n  \"theme\": \"dark\"\n}\nHas identity values: true\n\n=== IDENTITY.md exactly at cap (2097152 bytes) ===\nResult name: Proof Agent | Has identity values: true\n\n=== Oversized IDENTITY.md (2097153 bytes = cap + 1) ===\nloadAgentIdentityFromWorkspace result: null\nTreated as missing (returns null): true\nreadRegularFileSync threw: File exceeds 2097152 bytes: <tmp-workspace>/IDENTITY.md\n\nRemoved temp workspace. Standalone proof complete.\n```\n\nThe oversized file (2 MiB + 1, larger than `MAX_WORKSPACE_BOOTSTRAP_FILE_BYTES`) is rejected by the bounded reader with `File exceeds 2097152 bytes`, and the loader returns `null` — the agent falls back to no custom identity instead of buffering the file. Files at or under the cap load and parse exactly as before.\n\n### Focused regression tests (exact head)\n\n```text\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/identity-file.test.ts --run\n[test] starting test/vitest/vitest.agents.config.ts\n\n RUN  v4.1.9 <worktree>\n\n ✓ |agents| src/agents/identity-file.test.ts (10 tests) 299ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  10 passed (10)\n   Duration  2.67s\n\n[test] passed 1 Vitest shard in 9.75s\n```\n\nThis includes `returns null when IDENTITY.md exceeds the size cap`, which writes `MAX_WORKSPACE_BOOTSTRAP_FILE_BYTES + 1` bytes and asserts the `null` fallback.\n",
        "branch": "fix/bound-identity-file-read",
